<BaseLayout title="About MathGraph — Open verification infrastructure" description="MathGraph is open verification and trust infrastructure developed by Metalogic Labs." currentPath="/about/">
  <header class="section section--compact"><div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1>Evidence should remain inspectable without the platform that published it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">MathGraph is open verification and trust infrastructure developed by Metalogic Labs. It publishes source-pinned records, explicit verification boundaries, portable replay contracts, and visible unknowns.</p>
  </div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell grid"><div class="span-7 prose">
    <h2>Protocol first, applications optional.</h2>
    <p>MathGraph.org is one publisher and reader of the open contracts. Independent consumers can inspect exact historic evidence without relying on a hosted MathGraph service. Native verifiers retain authority within their declared scope.</p>
    <p>The current foundation is deliberately bounded: two immutable public records, offline consumers, advisory Discover output, and one qualified finite capability profile. Broader verification, current applicability, and autonomous development remain separate research obligations.</p>
  </div><aside class="span-5 callout"><strong>No endorsement implied.</strong><p>Public third-party source material is credited for provenance. MathGraph does not claim affiliation with or endorsement by the cited projects or institutions.</p></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
